        "bdb068b21e6e4b8b4342267e8d1cef232e6792de"
      ],
      "title": "SNMP: Remove uses of length -1 to tvb_memdup",
      "message": "SNMP: Remove uses of length -1 to tvb_memdup\n\nThe SNMP dissector is the only dissector using tvb_memdup with a length\nof -1 to mean \"to the end of the buffer.\" The lengths are explicitly\ncalculated in all cases immediately before it, so just use that.\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2025-12-12T20:57:11.000-05:00",
      "committer_name": "John Thacker",
      "committer_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2025-12-12T20:58:12.000-05:00",
